Go ahead and scream.

134
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,800
Let's see if anyone answers.

135
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,080
Deep in the mountains...

136
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,880
Who's gonna hear you?

137
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:12,760
Scream as loud as you can.

138
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,560
Go on, scream.

139
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,880
Hurry up and scream.

140
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,560
Why did you stop?

141
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,640
Scream!

142
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,720
This kid we got this time...

143
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,880
So pale and tender.

144
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,320
He'll definitely fetch a good price.

145
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,480
He's pale and tender, sure...

146
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,120
But the kid's a bit too old.

147
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,640
Howling like a banshee.

148
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,320
Let's just cut his tongue out.

149
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,320
Just to be safe.

150
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,120
Get him drunk. Let's see how he screams then.

151
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,920
If we really can't sell him...

152
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,920
I'll just keep him for myself.

153
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:41,320
Take him to the street to beg for money.

154
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,480
Xiwa!

155
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,640
Where did you go?

156
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,120
Grandma is so sorry.

157
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,520
Grandma lost you.

158
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,360
Grandma!

159
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,520
Let me out!

160
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,080
You hear that?

161
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:07,800
You hear that?

162
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,440
That silly kid fusses as soon as he wakes up.

163
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,240
Fusses the moment he wakes up.

164
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:11,200
I told you before...

165
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,480
Cut off his tongue.

166
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,920
You're too heavy-handed.

167
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,400
What if you kill him?

168
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,080
Let him cry for a couple of days.

169
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,440
He'll stop once he's tired out.

170
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,120
Those other kids...

171
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,840
Which of them didn't go through this?

172
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,920
Grandma!

173
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,480
Grandma!

174
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,160
Grandma!

175
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,320
Grandma!

176
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,080
Grandma!

177
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:45,160
Grandma!

178
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,280
Grandma!

179
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,160
Grandma!

180
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,760
Grandma!

181
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,200
Can't even let me sleep in peace!

182
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,600
If you keep crying...

183
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,280
I'll throw you in the dog pen to feed the dogs!

184
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,120
Hear me?

185
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:07,120
Xiwa!

186
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:10,040
Come home!

187
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:14,000
Xiwa!

188
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,000
Where did you go?

189
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:24,960
You little son of a bitch!

190
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,960
Running away from me?

191
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:27,560
You little son of a bitch!

192
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,320
You dare to run!

193
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,280
Stop!

194
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:06,800
Help!

195
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:08,920
Let me go!

196
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:09,960
Let me go!

197
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,360
Let me go!

198
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,440
Let me go!

199
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,240
Let me go!

200
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,160
Son of a bitch, you bit me!

201
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,160
I'll kill you!

202
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:20,680
You wanna run?

203
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:21,760
Run!

204
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,880
I'll teach you to run!

205
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,080
Run!

206
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,440
Son of a bitch, run!

207
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,240
I'll teach you to run!

208
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:29,960
Run!

209
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,320
Son of a bitch!

210
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:33,680
Run!

211
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:34,480
Try running again!

212
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,760
Run!

213
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,280
I'll teach you to run!

214
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,080
If any of you dare to run again,

215
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,320
you'll end up just like him.

216
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,440
I'll break your legs too!

217
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,880
Run!

218
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:43,520
Run!

219
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:45,160
Run!

220
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,280
Xiwa!

221
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,840
Xiwa!

222
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,800
Just like that girl from last time.

223
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,120
Croaked.

224
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,800
What are you mumbling about?

225
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,320
Go find an old straw mat.

226
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,400
Bury her under the vegetables.

227
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,560
What I saw...

228
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,760
That's pretty much it.

229
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,360
Those damn human traffickers...

230
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:13,800
...deserve to be hacked to pieces.

231
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,920
And rot in hell.

232
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,880
I saw them driving a van,

233
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,200
but I didn't catch the license plate.

234
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,720
The traffickers were all unfamiliar faces.

235
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,440
Twenty years have passed.

236
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,960
They must look completely different now.

237
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,920
There was one guy.

238
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:38,320
He had a character tattooed on his right wrist.

239
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,520
It was the character for "endurance."

240
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,040
Let's go to the police.

241
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,880
The problem is, it's been twenty years.

242
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,400
Do you think the police will believe it?

243
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,040
But this is a matter of life and death!

244
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,680
Whether they believe it or not, we have to try.

245
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,120
True.

246
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,000
Why is God so blind?

247
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,120
There are so many innocent people...

248
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,000
What goes around always comes around.

249
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,400
It's not a matter of if,

250
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,400
but when.

251
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:11,800
It's just poor Xizi.

252
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,800
He was so young.

253
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,000
Maybe,

254
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,200
with Grandma always talking about and remembering Xizi,

255
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,320
it's another way for him to live on.

256
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:25,200
Do you guys believe in a parallel world?

257
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,040
Throughout a person's life,

258
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,200
everyone has their own regrets.

259
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:33,360
Perhaps in another parallel world,

260
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,600
there are no bad guys.

261
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,240
Xizi was never abducted.

262
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:42,640
And Grandma now has a house full of kids and grandkids.

263
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:46,920
Bro.

264
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,240
Your childhood name

265
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,480
is also Xizi.

266
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:51,880
Maybe,

267
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,200
in some parallel world,

268
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,040
you are Granny Xiufang's grandson.

269
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:27,320
Chen Baixi.

270
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,520
Stop following me.

271
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,600
You want me to lie.

272
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,480
No way.

273
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:38,000
It's not deception.

274
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,040
It's giving.

275
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,320
You...

276
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,000
Isn't acting your greatest passion?

277
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:43,600
You told us yourself.

278
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,040
The art of acting is about

279
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,160
being able to interpret another person's life.

280
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:48,480
For an actor,

281
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:51,240
isn't that the happiest and most meaningful thing?

282
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,800
But that's on a film set.

283
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,760
When the director yells "cut,"

284
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:56,440
everyone leaves.

285
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,520
It's all fake.

286
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,320
But what does Grandma want?

287
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:01,400
Grandma wants it to never end.

288
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,200
Just imagine it.

289
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,280
Grandma waits at that big gate every day,

290
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:10,000
eagerly waiting for Xizi to come back.

291
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,760
So what am I giving her in the end?

292
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,280
An illusion.

293
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:16,920
Yes.

294
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,400
Your performance is fake.

295
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,280
But her fading hope is real.

296
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,360
The door she watches over is real.

297
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,920
Every single day she waits at that door.

298
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,560
Waiting for a Xizi who can never return is real, too.

299
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:34,600
I can't force you to do anything.

300
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,320
But

301
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,800
I think doing this

302
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,600
can at least, in her limited time left,

303
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:42,680
do as much as possible

304
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:44,880
to make up for her regrets and sorrow.

305
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:52,600
Chen Baixi.

306
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,520
In my eyes,

307
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,200
acting isn't about deception.

308
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,400
It's about daring to give your true feelings.

309
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,200
This is my plan.

310
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:45,680
Baixi,

311
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,880
have you really thought this through?

312
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:48,760
I have.

313
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,600
I think Yiran is right.

314
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,400
What does she have to do with this?

315
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,160
Granny Xiufang doesn't have another twenty years.

316
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,480
I don't want her to pass away with any regrets.

317
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:04,080
But this isn't going to be that easy.

318
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:06,960
You forgot,

319
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:08,680
I studied acting.

320
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,760
Then,

321
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,760
how will you make Grandma believe you're the real Xizi?

322
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:16,760
That's why

323
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,960
I'm asking for your help.

324
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:19,760
Sure.

325
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:29,360
Yiran,

326
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:32,400
you guys are trying to ruin my shop's reputation.

327
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:35,280
This face with this hairstyle...

328
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,200
It's practically a crime.

329
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,880
Go mess with someone else.

330
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:39,760
Come on,

331
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:40,560
Auntie Juan,

332
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,560
let's just treat this as a last-ditch effort.

333
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:51,760
Auntie Juan,

334
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:54,360
just do it.

335
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,440
I have an idea.

336
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,360
Does he look like him?

337
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,320
Yeah, he does.

338
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:11,560
Xiwa.

339
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:16,160
Grandma finally found you.

340
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:23,240
Grandma has gotten so old.

341
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:28,680
I don't know

342
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:33,560
if you still recognize Grandma.

343
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,280
Xiwa.

344
00:20:58,360 --> 00:20:59,640
My Xiwa,

345
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:05,560
you must have grown so tall.

346
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:11,160
I wonder if Grandma will still recognize you.

347
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,280
It's been 20 years.

348
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,520
Xiwa,

349
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,000
Grandma is here today

350
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,200
to take you home.

351
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:28,800
Xiwa,

352
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,560
come home.

353
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:36,800
Let's stick to the plan.

354
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,360
We start recording in three minutes.

355
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,640
All departments, get ready.

356
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:41,560
Okay, okay.

357
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:42,320
Director Ma,

358
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:45,680
here's today's rundown.

359
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,600
I'm counting on you.

360
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:47,200
Okay, okay.

361
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,040
Thanks for your hard work.

362
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:49,080
Xiao Li,

363
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:49,640
the car is almost here.

364
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,440
Go wait at the entrance.

365
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,000
Okay.

366
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,280
Don't put the flowers here.

367
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,080
Put them on the side.

368
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:55,760
Who left these here?

369
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,080
You can't hang the firecrackers here.

370
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,040
Hang them at the entrance.

371
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,120
We made it, we made it!

372
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,640
Of course we made it.

373
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,760
I thought we were going to be late.

374
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:03,440
Put it here.

375
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,680
Okay.

376
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:06,560
That works, that works.

377
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,200
Let's stand opposite each other.

378
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:09,040
Everyone, grab a couple more of these later.

379
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:09,480
Looks good.

380
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,240
Yiran.

381
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:10,760
Director Ma.

382
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:11,680
You guys made it too, right?

383
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:12,240
Here you go.

384
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:12,600
Confetti poppers.

385
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,000
Pop them later to liven things up.

386
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,800
Got it, got it.

387
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,640
Director Ma.

388
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,280
Come here.

389
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:18,240
Sister Xiufang.

390
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:19,960
Director Ma.

391
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,680
Xizi is already on his way.

392
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:22,680
He'll be here soon.

393
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:23,560
Great, great.

394
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:26,960
I haven't worn these clothes in years.

395
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:29,080
They don't look good anymore.

396
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:29,960
You look great.

397
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:30,960
Very beautiful.

398
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:33,880
When he arrives, keep the camera on him.

399
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:34,680
Pan over like this.

400
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,040
Then we'll shoot this whole scene.

401
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,960
They made this look so real.

402
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,760
Even the TV station staff are here.

403
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:49,360
Yiran,

404
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,560
look at this grand setup.

405
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:52,360
Hiring all these actors for this show.

406
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:53,440
It's really not easy.

407
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,920
Your brother said,

408
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:57,360
In for a penny, in for a pound.

409
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:59,160
We can't cut any corners.

410
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,960
Or it'll all be for nothing.

411
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,680
I mean, this brother of mine,

412
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,680
he really looks the part when he gets to work.

413
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:10,560
Dear viewers,

414
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:13,360
welcome to the Touching Moments program.

415
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,640
The recovery rate for abducted people is three in a thousand.

416
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:19,040
Today, we are that three in a thousand.

417
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:21,080
After a 20-year search,

418
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:24,760
with the joint efforts of all departments and volunteers,

419
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:27,560
today we will witness a miracle.

420
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,480
After being abducted for 20 years, Xizi

421
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:33,280
is finally returning to Granny Xiufang today.

422
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:36,080
Let's witness this thrilling moment together.

423
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:50,560
Grandma.

424
00:24:51,360 --> 00:24:52,160
My child.

425
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:07,040
It's my boy.

426
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:09,080
Grandma said,

427
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:11,960
this teardrop mole wards off disaster.

428
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,280
My Xiwa is blessed.

429
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:21,200
Grandma,

430
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:24,360
do you remember this scar?

431
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,160
When I was little, I climbed a tree

432
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,160
and accidentally fell,

433
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,280
leaving this mark.

434
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:31,080
And because you were afraid I'd get a beating,

435
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:33,040
you kept it a secret.

436
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,040
Xiwa,

437
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:41,360
Grandma is so sorry.

438
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:43,960
It's all my fault.

439
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,600
I lost you.

440
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:53,840
My boy.

441
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:57,880
Grandma, I...

442
00:25:57,880 --> 00:25:58,560
I'm back.

443
00:25:58,560 --> 00:25:59,960
I'll never leave again.

444
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:04,960
Oh heavens, you've brought my Xiwa

445
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:09,160
back to me.

446
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,360
Grandma, don't cry.

447
00:26:16,080 --> 00:26:19,200
It's all my fault. I lost you.

448
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,800
I can't watch this.

449
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,120
I need a moment.

450
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,160
Call me if you need me.

451
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:36,160
Dear viewers,

452
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,560
this is the power of family.

453
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:38,680
It's the power of love.

454
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:40,080
No matter how much time passes,

455
00:26:40,080 --> 00:26:41,400
no matter how great the distance,

456
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:43,600
family will always bring you home.

457
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:44,960
After twenty years,

458
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:46,960
Xizi has come home.

459
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,360
Child.

460
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:08,120
Come.

461
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:09,840
Have some water.

462
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,280
Have a seat.

463
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,120
Child.

464
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:23,560
Tell Grandma

465
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,000
how you've been all these years.

466
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:31,400
Back then, at the market,

467
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:33,280
the traffickers took me away.

468
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:37,200
They sold me to a place very, very far away,

469
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:39,160
a remote mountain village.

470
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:42,160
Grandma, Grandma.

471
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,360
I didn't suffer.

472
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,960
My adoptive parents were very good to me.

473
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:47,360
They even paid for my college.

474
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:50,280
After graduation, I missed you so much,

475
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:51,600
and Mom and Dad.

476
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,080
So I kept searching for you.

477
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:55,840
Thankfully, through the TV station,

478
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,440
I finally made it back home.

479
00:27:58,280 --> 00:27:59,440
You've grown up.

480
00:28:04,360 --> 00:28:07,280
If your dad and your mom

481
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:09,280
knew you were back,

482
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:12,760
they would be so happy.

483
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:25,360
Tragically,

484
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,360
when you went missing,

485
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:32,040
they drove out to look for you.

486
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:34,640
On the way,

487
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:36,760
they got into a car crash,

488
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:39,680
and they both passed away.

489
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:47,240
It's all my fault.

490
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:52,560
If I

491
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,960
hadn't lost you,

492
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,240
our family

493
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:02,880
wouldn't have ended up like this.

494
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:06,200
The four of us...

495
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:08,440
It would have been so nice.

496
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:17,480
Grandma,

497
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:19,880
it's all in the past now.

498
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:21,480
My darling,

499
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,440
Xiwa has been found.

500
00:29:26,680 --> 00:29:28,160
The two of you

501
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:31,880
in the afterlife,

502
00:29:32,360 --> 00:29:34,120
please watch over him.

503
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:38,560
Keep him safe and sound.

504
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:41,680
Child...

505
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:45,480
My child...

506
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:09,560
Oh, right.

507
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:10,760
This is for you.

508
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:12,720
A lipstick.

509
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:14,600
Did you forget already?

510
00:30:15,560 --> 00:30:16,760
When you came back,

511
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,760
my alpaca broke it.

512
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:32,880
What are you doing here?

513
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:34,960
I'm doing a good deed.

514
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,200
Is that a crime?

515
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:41,440
I heard you convinced Chen Baixi to help.

516
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,200
I wouldn't say I convinced him.

517
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,400
I just said a few words.

518
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:46,600
He mostly figured it out on his own.

519
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:47,960
Looks like

520
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:50,000
I underestimated you.

521
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:54,760
A lot of people underestimate me.

522
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,200
Get in line.

523
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:13,600
Officer.

524
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:14,640
These are the clues and evidence we compiled

525
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:17,960
for that trafficking case from twenty years ago.

526
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:21,480
Most of them are details that Granny Xiufang recalled.

527
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:22,960
According to her recollection,

528
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:25,880
the trafficker did have a unique tattoo on his wrist.

529
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:33,200
The statute of limitations for this case has expired.

530
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:35,800
Alright.

531
00:31:35,800 --> 00:31:37,680
We'll update our files

532
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,600
and reopen the investigation.

533
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:39,800
We're counting on you.

534
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:42,280
This means a great deal to Zhang Xiufang's family.

535
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:43,800
Understood.

536
00:31:44,600 --> 00:31:46,280
We'll notify you as soon as there's any news.

537
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:48,120
Thank you for providing this information.

538
00:32:36,040 --> 00:32:36,920
Sister Xiufang.

539
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,200
You're looking great!

540
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:40,640
Director Ma, right?

541
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:41,520
Yes.

542
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:44,040
My grandson.

543
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:45,800
The TV station found him.

544
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:47,040
That's wonderful! That's great!

545
00:32:47,040 --> 00:32:48,440
Such a good grandson.

546
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:51,000
Xiwa made this.

547
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:51,440
Try some.

548
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:52,240
Alright, alright.

549
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:53,000
Thank you.

550
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:54,400
Enjoy your walk, then.

551
00:32:54,600 --> 00:32:55,440
Goodbye, Director Ma.

552
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,680
Take care.

553
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:00,720
Okay.

554
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:01,760
Alright.

555
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,080
Auntie Xiufang.

556
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:05,880
It's been a while.

557
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:06,600
Is this...

558
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:08,480
My grandson.

559
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:10,200
He's back.

560
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,480
That's wonderful.

561
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,160
Wow...

562
00:33:13,440 --> 00:33:15,800
I don't even know how to congratulate you.

563
00:33:16,080 --> 00:33:17,200
That's great, really great.

564
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:18,520
What a good kid.

565
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:19,320
Auntie Zhao.

566
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:20,800
He sure is.

567
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:23,000
My grandson made this.

568
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:24,000
Have a taste.

569
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,000
Brown sugar glutinous rice cakes.

570
00:33:25,040 --> 00:33:26,000
They're delicious.

571
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,600
Then I must share in the joy.

572
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:29,880
We'll be going now.

573
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:30,880
Okay, okay.

574
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:31,520
Goodbye.

575
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:32,440
Hope business goes well!

576
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:33,480
Thank you, thank you.

577
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:34,160
Good boy.

578
00:33:35,520 --> 00:33:36,880
Grandma, what else do you want to see?

579
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:37,680
Let's see.

580
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:38,080
Let's look ahead.

581
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:38,680
Over there.

582
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,840
Do you remember?

583
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:42,120
Grandma.

584
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:43,200
Time to eat.

585
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:00,480
Grandma, what's wrong?

586
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:02,520
Is the food not to your taste?

587
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:07,960
My child...

588
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:10,840
It's been twenty years.

